# Grid A — S5 Enumerate (interface implementations)
#
# Targets: generic scenario + ShapeListOfSymbols + ReqEnumeration.
# Validates that the pipeline returns the SET of identifiers
# implementing a named interface, not a prose summary or a count.
#
# Ground truth (internal/agent/loop_policy.go): LoopController is the
# optional interface agents implement. The set of implementers is
# small and grep-discoverable. Positive anchor is the interface name
# itself (must appear in any correct enumeration answer to establish
# grounding). Negative anchors block Java-distribution leaks and the
# "Evaluator" drift mode (a sibling interface that sometimes
# contaminates the answer when the LLM conflates interfaces).
ID="s5a"
NAME="enumerate — LoopController implementers"
QUESTION="列出本仓库里所有实现了 LoopController 接口的具体类型，逐个给出类型名和所在文件。"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous EC was just `LoopController`
# (the interface name in the question itself) — bar = "复述题目"
# 即可 PASS, no enumeration verification. Ground truth (verified via
# `rg -n 'func \\(e \\*.*Evaluator\\) Observe\\(' internal/agent/`):
# 8 concrete LoopController implementers — analyzerEvaluator /
# answerDocumentEvaluator / explorerEvaluator / extractorEvaluator /
# logTriagerEvaluator / perfTriagerEvaluator / subExplorerEvaluator /
# writeAnalyzerEvaluator. coder/planner/verifier have ShouldStop hooks but do
# not implement LoopController because they do not define Observe. Strict-bar
# requires AT LEAST 4
# distinct implementer names verbatim — generic prose "several
# Evaluator types implement it" no longer PASSes.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="LoopController"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="(analyzerEvaluator|analyzer_evaluator)
(explorerEvaluator|explorer_evaluator)
(extractorEvaluator|extractor_evaluator)
(answerDocumentEvaluator|finalizer.*[Ee]valuator|answer_document_evaluator)"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS=".java .py Evaluator.java BaseAgent.java"
